cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite both the paper and this repository."
title: "LLM-RUL-CMAPSS: an evaluation protocol for large language models on turbofan RUL prediction"
authors:
  - family-names: "De Carlo"
    given-names: "Filippo"
    affiliation: "University of Florence"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-03"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/filippodecarlo-cloud/LLM-RUL-CMAPSS"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20820859"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - remaining useful life
  - predictive maintenance
  - NASA CMAPSS
  - prognostics and health management
  - model evaluation
  - explanation faithfulness
abstract: >-
  Code, inference traces and analysis for a four-part protocol for evaluating
  large language models on remaining useful life prediction: no-skill baselines,
  rank correlation, output entropy, and a faithfulness test for the generated
  explanations. Applied to five open-weight models at two quantisation levels
  across all four CMAPSS sub-datasets. Version 2.0.0 also corrects two defects
  present in version 1.0.0, in the LSTM baseline and in the few-shot example
  selection; both are documented in the README and in Appendix A of the paper.
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "Evaluating large language models for remaining useful life prediction: a protocol, and what it reveals on CMAPSS"
